  "body": "Filing status memo per the 19:00 brief's §10 (status reporting expected back). **Track A packaging complete; PO action required for the final submission step.** **What shipped:** Repo `github.com/catdef/catdef-plugin` created (public, MIT). Initial commit `e641be2` pushed under provisional `canonical-implementor <canonical-implementor@catdef.org>` identity. Contents per the 19:00 brief, strategic shape unchanged: `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` (name=catdef, version=1.4.0, author=catdef-maintainer@catdef.org per CA-009, MIT, homepage=catdef.org); `.mcp.json` with `type=http` + `url=https://catdef.org/mcp` per the canonical surface; three `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` files (validate, scaffold, extract) with YAML frontmatter authored to trigger Claude auto-invocation on the trigger phrases in the brief; `spec/` vendored snapshot of CATDEF_SPEC.md / CATIO_SPEC.md / MCP_REFERENCE.md / CONTRIBUTING.md / canonical reference catalog (per brief's vendor-snapshot recommendation); README.md using the Director-edited listing copy verbatim; LICENSE (MIT, matches catdef-spec); standard .gitignore. **Open verification questions, status:** Q1 (.mcp.json remote-MCP schema) RESOLVED via WebFetch on code.claude.com/docs/en/mcp — `type=http` + `url=...` is canonical; OAuth/headers/timeout fields available if needed. Q2 (graceful-degradation when server unreachable) RESOLVED by same docs: Claude Code retries with exponential backoff, marks failed servers as failed, skills function independently regardless. Documented in README's MCP-surface section. Q3 (CI auto-bump granularity) DEFERRED — resolves post-submission when pin behavior becomes observable; not a packaging blocker. Q4 (catdef.org DNS commitment) CONFIRMED by Director: pointable + active; Railway auto-deploy on push to catdef.org repo. **Tactical choices made within the brief's tactical-freedom scope:** (a) vendored snapshot rather than git submodule (per brief recommendation); (b) `conformance/` vendored as a pointer README + spec text rather than the full pytest suite, since rule-based validation in the SKILL.md is the v0 shape and mechanical validation moves to catdef.org/mcp's `catdef_validate` tool; (c) SKILL.md content authored as informative and triage-friendly rather than terse — each has trigger criteria, procedure, do-not-do guardrails, and reference paths; (d) README structure follows brief §6 sketch with light expansion. **What I did NOT do (out of scope or PO-side):** `claude plugin validate` local run — the `claude` CLI is not on this host's PATH; PO can run it from inside Claude Code or a terminal with the CLI installed; manifest is hand-validated for parse + required fields. Marketplace submission via the web form at claude.ai/settings/plugins/submit — this is a browser/UI action; needs PO to walk it through. **What's queued from this seat:** CA-008 Directive 3 — build the catdef.org/mcp server in the catdef.org/ repo. PO authorized both Track A and the server build at session start. Plugin ship does not block on server existence (per CA-008 + the 19:00 brief), so the server build proceeds in parallel on its own clock. **Flagging for strategist consideration (not action-required from strategist):** I used `canonical-implementor <canonical-implementor@catdef.org>` as a provisional bot identity for the initial commit. No prior commits in the catdef.org/ repo have used a seat-bound bot identity (all prior canonical-implementor work was attributed to Scott directly). Following the same provisional-then-ratified pattern that produced CA-009 (where strategist + maintainer identities were ratified retroactively for CA-001/007/008), a future strategist session may want to consider whether to ratify `canonical-implementor@catdef.org` as the third canonical seat identity. Not blocking anything; just legible if/when a CA-NNN housekeeping decision rolls up identity decisions. **Standing posture:** Plugin work hands off to PO for marketplace submission; this seat continues to the server build. Status memos for milestone (b) Anthropic-review-approved-or-rejected and (c) plugin-appears-in-catalog will follow on PO trigger (PO files when submission happens, then again when status changes are observable in claude-plugins-community repo).",

